  "notes": "Walk cost is O(|V| * d): for each lattice vertex we run the per-axis forward (plus optional backward for directed+mutual) emission. Throughput stays in the 20-33 Medge/s band across shapes — the 2-D torus tax (extra wrap edges + branchy carry) pulls the per-edge cost up vs the non-periodic grid, and directed+mutual adds the symmetric back-arc pass for a ~2/3 throughput. 3-D pays for the deeper carry/coords walk but stays comparable per emitted edge. No allocator hot path: the edges Vec grows linearly; Graph::new + add_edges dominates the post-walk cost on large shapes."
